# Docker build context for the REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# Exactly one build uses this context: public-web/deploy/Dockerfile, which needs
# the repository root because build.mjs cross-checks the claim register against
# both the living CSV and the frozen v0.2 package under docs/public/. Every other
# surface builds from its own directory with its own .dockerignore
# (backend/, platform-admin-web/).
#
# WHY THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST.
#
# The previous denylist version was measured, and what it let through was not a
# tidiness problem:
#
#   - .agent-runtime/ holds 88 git worktrees, 1,089,727 files, and 201 .env*
#     files including a real parent-web/.env. `.env` in a denylist matches only
#     the ROOT .env, so every nested one was in the context.
#   - .env.azure sits at the repository root with six populated values including
#     a database password. `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.*.local` all fail to
#     match it -- `.env.*.local` requires a `.local` suffix. It is gitignored, so
#     it was never at risk of being committed, but gitignore has no bearing on
#     what Docker sends to the daemon.
#   - .claude/ and .vs/ carry local session and IDE state.
#   - android/, ios/, parent-web/, contracts/, tooling/ are megabytes of material
#     no image needs.
#
# A denylist has to anticipate every one of those. An allowlist only has to name
# what the build actually reads, and anything added to the repository later is
# excluded by default rather than included by default. For a context that is sent
# whole to the daemon, default-deny is the only version that stays correct.

# Exclude everything...
*

# ...then re-admit exactly what public-web/deploy/Dockerfile COPYs.
!public-web
!docs/public/PCA_PUBLIC_CLAIM_REGISTER.csv
!docs/public/PCA_Public_Programme_Documentation_Package_v0.2/PCA_PUBLIC_CLAIM_REGISTER.csv

# ...minus the parts of public-web that are build output or local state. These
# are re-excluded AFTER the re-admission above, because later patterns win.
public-web/dist
public-web/reports
public-web/node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.publishsettings
**/id_rsa*
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
